# Copy to .env (git-ignored). Loaded with: set -a; . ./.env; set +a
# Values go between double quotes, one per line. Nothing here is ever committed.
#
# Who reads what:
#   Foundry scripts (contracts:deploy, demo:*)  → SEPOLIA_RPC_URL, DEPLOYER_*, WETH_ADDRESS, MOOR_* (passed inline)
#   Live App (pnpm dev)                         → nothing; it uses a public RPC unless NEXT_PUBLIC_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL is set
#   Agent, on this machine only (pnpm agent)    → SEPOLIA_RPC_URL, AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, AGENT_*
#   Agent, on the VPS                           → none of this file: apps/agent/deploy/run.sh reads the secrets from Ledger Key Ring

# Sepolia JSON-RPC endpoint. For the agent it must allow wide eth_getLogs ranges:
# PublicNode (https://ethereum-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com) does; Alchemy's free tier allows 10 blocks.
SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=""

# Deployer: paid for Aqua/SwapVM, MoorRegistrar and the holder's proxies. Test funds only.
DEPLOYER_ADDRESS=""
DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=""
# Optional: an existing WETH on the target chain. When empty, Deploy.s.sol deploys TestWETH.
WETH_ADDRESS=""

# The agent's hot key: ROLE_SET_TEXT on the eight moor.agent.* keys and nothing else (05 §7).
# Needs a little Sepolia ETH for one multicall per position per cycle.
AGENT_ADDRESS=""
AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY=""

# Claude Opus 5 for the proposals. Optional: without it the agent writes the deterministic proposal.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
# Only if the key is not scoped to a workspace (console.anthropic.com → Settings → Workspaces → ID, wrkspc_…)
ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=""

# Agent knobs (all optional; defaults in apps/agent/src/env.ts)
# AGENT_PARENT_NAME="salviega.eth"     the holder's name; positions are its subnames
# AGENT_INTERVAL_SECONDS="300"
# AGENT_MODEL="claude-opus-5"
# AGENT_LOGS_CHUNK="10000"             eth_getLogs range per request
# AGENT_FROM_BLOCK="11600000"          first block to scan for position names
# AGENT_DRY_RUN="1"                    read, derive and log — send nothing
# AGENT_FORCE_PROPOSE="1"              ask the model again even if a proposal for the same trigger is standing (testing)

# Live App (optional): a private RPC for the deployed app; inlined at build time on Vercel
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=""
